file: src/Hyperdrive/HTTP1/Framing.hs

why: an HTTP/1.0 message with Transfer-Encoding has faulty framing (RFC 9112 Section 6.1)
- | not (null te), version < HTTP_1_1 = Left TransferEncodingInHTTP10
+ | False = Left TransferEncodingInHTTP10

why: Transfer-Encoding with Content-Length is the request smuggling pattern, rejected
- | not (null te), not (null cl)      = Left BothLengthAndEncoding
+ | False      = Left BothLengthAndEncoding

why: the chunked coding has no parameters (RFC 9112 Section 7.1)
- | params                          -> Left ChunkedWithParameters
+ | False                           -> Left ChunkedWithParameters

why: chunked may only be applied once (RFC 9112 Section 6.1)
- | any ((== "chunked") . fst) earlier -> Left ChunkedTwice
+ | False -> Left ChunkedTwice

why: only chunked is supported; any other coding gets 501
- | ((c, _) : _) <- reverse earlier  -> Left (UnsupportedTransferCoding c)
+ | ((c, _) : _) <- reverse earlier, c == "gzip"  -> Left (UnsupportedTransferCoding c)

why: transfer coding names are case-insensitive
- Right (C.map toLower name, not (B.null rest))
+ Right (name, not (B.null rest))

why: whitespace is allowed around the "=" of a transfer-parameter (BWS)
- Just (0x3D, s3) -> value (B.dropWhile isOWS s3) >>= params
+ Just (0x3D, s3) -> value s3 >>= params

why: a transfer-parameter needs a value
- in if B.null t then Left InvalidTransferEncoding else Right rest
+ in Right rest

why: a list of lengths is accepted only when every value is the same
- Just (n : ns) | all (== n) ns -> Right n
+ Just (n : _) -> Right n

why: a length too large for 64 bits is invalid, not wrapped around
- if n > (maxBound - d) `div` 10 then Nothing else Just (n * 10 + d)
+ Just (n * 10 + d)

why: 501 is for a coding the server does not support; every other framing error is 400
- framingErrorStatus (UnsupportedTransferCoding _) = NotImplemented
+ framingErrorStatus (UnsupportedTransferCoding _) = BadRequest

why: a 204 has no body and no framing fields (RFC 9110 8.6, RFC 9112 6.1)
- | status == NoContent || status == NotModified = HeaderOnly Nothing
+ | status == NotModified = HeaderOnly Nothing

why: a 304 has no body, and its 200's length is unknown
- | status == NoContent || status == NotModified = HeaderOnly Nothing
+ | status == NoContent = HeaderOnly Nothing

why: a 2xx to CONNECT has no framing fields; only 2xx opens a tunnel
- | method == CONNECT, statusClass status == Successful = HeaderOnly Nothing
+ | method == CONNECT = HeaderOnly Nothing

why: a response to HEAD has no body
- | method == HEAD = HeaderOnly (payload >>= payloadLength)
+ | False = HeaderOnly (payload >>= payloadLength)

why: a known length without trailers is sent with Content-Length, not chunked
- Just (Payload (Just n) False) -> SendLength n
+ Just (Payload (Just n) False) | version < HTTP_1_1 -> SendLength n

why: Transfer-Encoding only for HTTP/1.1 requests (RFC 9112 6.1)
- | version >= HTTP_1_1    -> SendChunked
+ | True    -> SendChunked

why: an HTTP/1.0 client gets Content-Length when the length is known, not a close-delimited body
- | Just n <- len          -> SendLength n
+ | Just n <- len, n == 0  -> SendLength n

why: a response to HEAD sends the length GET would have sent
- HeaderOnly (Just n) -> [(hContentLength, decimal n)]
+ HeaderOnly (Just _) -> []
